{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1wscxiWmSVokFaBwSsR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I did not sign off. I found bugs in the toolbar list action and the new-file dialog, and I have not confirmed the fixes or the rest of the areas.\n\n**Confirmed (developer reproduced and logged):**\n- **Unordered list on an indented marker line:** on `  - child` (in Indent.md), the toolbar action produces `  - - child`. It adds a second marker instead of recognising the existing one. A top-level `- item` line toggles correctly.\n\n**Filed, but the developer could not reproduce:**\n- **New-file dialog, todo.txt type:** choosing todo.txt sets the extension field to `.todo.txt`. Plain Text gives `.txt`, and the other types give `.md`, `.adoc`, `.org`, `.csv` and `.txt` as expected. I reproduced this twice on screen. I can't tell whether `.todo.txt` is intended.\n- **Editor settings, \"Unordered list character\":** after choosing \"Asterisk (*)\" (it stays checked on reopen), the toolbar list action still inserted \"- \". The developer could not reproduce this. My steps may be incomplete, so this needs a second look.\n- **Dialog title:** the \"Unordered list character\" dialog is titled \"Theme\". The developer could not reproduce this either. It is visible on screen, so it is probably real.\n\n**Checked and working:**\n- Sort dialog: Date, Name, Folder first, Reverse order and .dotfiles all apply. Cancel discards the change. The choices persist across an app restart and survive rotation.\n- File browser: opening Zeta and going back works.\n- New-file dialog: Wikitext, AsciiDoc, OrgMode and CSV extensions are correct.\n- Editor: toggling the list marker off on a top-level line works, and \"- \" is inserted on a plain line.\n\n**Not covered:** the rest of the formatting toolbar (ordered list, bold, headings and so on), the Markdown-specific settings beyond the list character, and the search and Regex files.\n\nI left every test file unchanged: unsaved edits were undone or discarded, and Save is disabled on the last file I touched.\n\nI'm not signing off because the sign-off tool only accepts PASS, and I have open reports. The list-action and todo.txt issues are the ones to fix first."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4680, "cache_read_input_tokens": 360908, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4680}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3fa3431a-705d-4579-a9f7-ff922532fde2", "uuid": "2c28dbc2-c87e-42d8-b2fd-1c4871c7098c", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T01:24:00.388Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1wschqJGEoxNVBccGjh"}
